ed epel-release install and a broken rabbitmqadmin binary left in /usr/local/bin) were not cleaned up but pose low risk.","limitations":["Node2's post-restart recovery evidence relies on cluster/queue HTTP API state rather than an immediate dedicated publish/consume round-trip specific to that node, though overall functional recovery was later reconfirmed via node3.","The first node3 post-restart publish/consume attempt (cmd-056915ec768e4384) returned no message, likely due to a timing race after copying the password file; this was resolved on retry (cmd-f5d886a2c3b94c22), but the transient failure is noted for completeness.","Full package-manager consistency output and complete journalctl history are truncated in some captured evidence, limiting deep verification of underlying system health beyond what was reported."]},"ttft_ms":31564,"type":"result","duration_ms":80202,"uuid":"02cc5d8b-5398-41ec-9c37-0587bdcd88da","ttft_stream_ms":1611,"time_to_request_ms":47,"first_content_frame_ms":2156,"queued_turn_count":0}
